---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SpanChart from "../components/SpanChart.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { moments } from "../data/moments.js";
---
<Base title="When" dek="How far back each of the six families can be proved, and the biggest dated moments in all of them, in order.">

  <div class="hero" style="text-align:left">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--safrica)">How long ago</div>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(38px,7vw,70px)">When</h1>
      <p class="lead big">A number like 1750 does not mean much on its own. So here are all
      six families on one line, where you can see which of them reach back furthest — and then
      the biggest moments in all of them, in the order they really happened.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How far back we can prove</h2>
      <p class="lead">The solid bar starts at the oldest person we have a real date for.
      The faded part is older still — but it is reached through the mothers instead of the
      fathers, or it has not been properly checked yet.</p>
      <div class="mapwrap"><div class="scroll"><SpanChart /></div></div>
      <p class="cap">Six families and only about 130 years between the oldest and the youngest
      start. The Lerena bar is the short one because that research began most recently — not
      because the family is any younger.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--safrica)">In order</div>
      <h2>{moments.length} moments</h2>
      <div class="moments">
        {moments.map(m => (
          <div class={`moment c-${m.k} ${m.big ? "big" : ""}`}>
            <div class="my">{m.y}</div>
            <div>
              <div class="mt">{m.t}{m.age && <span class="agebadge">{m.age}</span>}</div>
              <p>{m.w}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--safrica)">Meanwhile</div>
      <h2>What the rest of the world was doing</h2>
      <p class="lead">It is hard to feel how long ago 1750 is. Here is what had not been invented yet.</p>
      <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:24px">
        <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--croatia);--cw:var(--croatia-wash);--cd:var(--croatia-deep)">
          <h3>When Giovanni was born, about 1750</h3>
          <p>There were no photographs, no railways, no electric light and no anaesthetic — if you
          needed an operation, you were awake for it. Mozart had not been born.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--safrica);--cw:var(--safrica-wash);--cd:var(--safrica-deep)">
          <h3>When the Nautilus sailed, 1819</h3>
          <p>Napoleon was still alive, in prison on a tiny island in the middle of the Atlantic —
          not very far from the route the ship was taking. He died two years later.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--safrica)">A big number</div>
      <h2>How many grandparents have you got?</h2>
      <p class="lead">Everybody has two parents. So everybody has four grandparents, and eight
      great-grandparents. It doubles every single time you go up a step.</p>
      <div class="doubling">
        {[["Parents",2],["Grandparents",4],["Great-grandparents",8],["2× great",16],["3× great",32],
          ["4× great",64],["5× great",128],["6× great",256],["7× great",512],["8× great",1024]].map(([lab,n]) => (
          <div class="dstep" style={`--w:${Math.max(4, (n/1024)*100)}%`}>
            <span class="dlab">{lab}</span>
            <span class="dbar"></span>
            <b>{n.toLocaleString("en-GB")}</b>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--italy);--cw:var(--italy-wash);--cd:var(--italy-deep);margin-top:24px">
        <h3>So think about Matteo Falco</h3>
        <p>He is your 8× great-grandpa, at the very top of the Falco ladder. That means there were
        <b>1,024 people</b> in his generation who all had to exist, and every single one of them had
        to meet somebody, or you would not be here. Matteo is just the one whose name we know.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pager">
        <a href={u("/")}>🌳 Back to the tree</a>
        <a href={u("/journeys/")}>How they all got here →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
